,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Belden Inc. provides connection solutions to bring data infrastructure into alignment to unlock new possibilities for its customers. The company provides copper cable and connectivity solutions, fiber cable and connectivity solutions, interconnect panels, racks and enclosures, and signal extension and matrix switching systems for use in local area networks, data centers, access control, 5G, fiber to the home, and building automation applications. It also provides power, cooling, and airflow management products for mission-critical data center operations; and end-to-end fiber and copper network systems. It also serves commercial real estate, education, financial institutions, stadiums and venues, military installations, and broadband and wireless service providers, as well as data centers, government, healthcare, and hospitality sectors. In addition, the company offers network digitization and automation solutions; and products and solutions covering various aspects of data handling, including acquisition, transmission, orchestration, and management for applications in discrete automation, process automation, energy, and mass transit. It sells its products to distributors, end-users, installers, and original equipment manufacturers (OEMs). It operates in the Americas, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and the Asia-Pacific. The company was formerly known as Belden CDT Inc. and changed its name to Belden Inc. in May 2007. Belden Inc. was founded in 1902 and is headquartered in Saint Louis, Missouri.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Ashish  Chand | President, CEO & Director | Age 50 | Compensation: $2.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 8K people. Revenue per employee of $339K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers. Each employee generates $27K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Belden Inc is a mid-cap technology business with a $3.6B market cap on $2.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years and +2% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 13% against a 9% cost of capital, a 4-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, with gross margins sitting at 36%.","The business throws off $219M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.49\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 7.3\u00d7.","Net dilution runs at 0.1% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.5\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (15.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Technology ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (43% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Sector under pressure with a 19.3% decline over the past 6 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 41% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Piotroski score 8/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","21 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Financial quality scores above most Technology peers"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(BDC) Price Dynamics and Execution-Aware Positioning","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/132/BDC_Price_Dynamics_and_Execution-Aware_Positioning_111826095802_1795057082.html","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795057082.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"$HAREHOLDER ALERT: The M&A Class Action Firm Announces An Investigation of Investcorp Credit Management BDC, Inc. (NASDAQ: ICMB)","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/hareholder-alert-the-ma-class-action-firm-announces-an-investigation-of-investc